COMMENT     REVIEWED REFSEQ: This record has been curated by NCBI staff. The
            reference sequence was derived from AL590031.6, AL669934.6 and
            AL512504.9.
            
            On or before Jun 7, 2025 this sequence version replaced
            XM_005262113.4, XM_054326752.1.
            
            Summary: The protein encoded by this gene contains a bromodomain
            and several WD repeats. It is thought to have a chromatin-modifying
            function, and may thus play a role in transcription. Mutations in
            this gene are associated with a spectrum of cognitive disabilities
            and X-linked macrocephaly. This gene is also associated with
            translocations in patients with B-cell chronic lymphocytic
            leukemia. [provided by RefSeq, Jul 2017].
            
